title Chats that message each other
sub Drawn from the intent before modeling: a chat sends another chat a message, may ask to be told when it answers, and no chain of chats waking chats outlives the user's message

== graph Chats that message each other
view: states
tone idle: Quiet
tone you: Working on your message
tone chat: Working on another chat's message
tone back: Working on an answer that came back
[*] -> quiet
group one: One chat
quiet: Quiet, waiting for you {idle}
yours: Working on what you wrote {you}
asked: Working on what another chat sent it {chat}
told: Working on another chat's answer, which came back {back}
group end
group done: Every chat
settled: Every chat quiet again, the answer came back once
  state: AllQuiet /\ Noticed # {}
group end
!loop: Chats keep waking each other after your message
  fails: BoundedChain
!twice: The same answer comes back twice
  fails: NoticeOnce
!early: Told before the other chat took the message in
  fails: NoticeAfterAnswer
quiet -> yours: you write
quiet -> asked: another chat sends it a message
quiet -> told: an answer it asked for comes back
yours -> asked: another chat's message joins the turn
yours -> told: the answer comes back during the turn
asked -> yours: you write during the turn
asked -> told: the answer comes back during the turn
told -> yours: you write during the turn
told -> asked: another chat's message joins the turn
yours -> quiet: it answers
asked -> quiet: it answers
told -> quiet: it answers
write: quiet > yours => quiet | you write | You write in a chat and it answers you there.
ask: quiet > asked => quiet | ask another chat | You ask the main chat to ask Reading something; Reading answers in Reading.
back: quiet > yours > quiet > told => quiet | told when done | The main chat asks Reading and asks to be told; when Reading answers, the answer comes back to the main chat, which answers you.
once: quiet > yours > quiet > told => settled | settles | After the answer comes back, every chat goes quiet: nothing sends again until you write.
